hich is equal  to one over two  now triangle a prime b prime c prime  has exactly the same area as triangle  abc  thus we have the same ratio for the area  of bdc  to the area of the triangle a prime b  prime c prime  from here suppose the overlapping region  bdc has an area equal to x  by the ratio of these areas the  remaining area  in triangle abc must also be equal to x  and then the remaining area in triangle  a prime b  prime c prime must also be equal to x  we can thus calculate the ratio of the  shaded area  to that of the entire shape it'll be  equal to x  over three x which is equal to one over  three  what's remarkable is this ratio is the  same  for all such right triangles that we  overlap  in this fashion as long as b prime is on  the x here  we have the same ratio of the shaded  area to the entire shape  as one over three and i think that's  quite beautiful  thanks for making us one of the best  communities on youtube  see you next episode of mind your  decisions where we solve the world's  problems  one video at a time  [Music]  you
 

